course: dictionary
lesson: 1794
title: Clockwise and anticlockwise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Clockwise is a word about direction. It means moving round in the same way as the hands of a clock: from the top, to the right, down, to the left and back up. «A right turn is a quarter turn clockwise» means a turn of a quarter of a circle, in the clock direction.
explain: The opposite is anticlockwise, which goes the other way round. Clockwise can work as an adverb, as in «turn clockwise», or as an adjective, as in «a clockwise direction». Context tells you which one you are reading.
explain: Read the clues around the word. Shepherds use «come by» for moving clockwise round the flock and «away to me» for anticlockwise. Ask yourself: which way would the words around this make things move? Then check your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Clockwise means round in the same direction as the hands of a clock.
fact: The opposite is anticlockwise (UK, Australia, New Zealand, Ireland) or counterclockwise (US, Canada).
fact: «Turn clockwise» and «a quarter turn clockwise» are phrases you will use in maths.
fact: In maths, a quarter turn is 90°, a half turn is 180° and a three-quarter turn is 270°.
fact: In everyday life, you usually turn a screw or jar lid clockwise to tighten it: «righty-tighty, lefty-loosey».
exercise: What does clockwise mean? | Moving straight up and down | *Moving round in the same direction as the hands of a clock | Moving very fast | Moving round the other way, against the hands of a clock
exercise: «A right turn is a quarter turn clockwise.» How many degrees is a quarter turn? | 180 | 270 | *90 | 360
exercise: What is the opposite of clockwise in the UK? | Upwards | *Anticlockwise | Clockwise | Sideways
test: If you face north and turn right twice, which way do you face? (Each right turn is a quarter turn clockwise.) | North | East | West | *South
test: «Each big ocean has huge circular currents called gyres, turning clockwise in the northern hemisphere.» Which way do these gyres turn in the northern hemisphere? | In no direction | Anticlockwise | Straight up | *Clockwise
exam: Mia says clockwise means a turn to the left. Is she right? | *No, clockwise goes from the top to the right, like the hands of a clock | Yes, clockwise means straight up | Yes, clockwise means a turn to the left | No, clockwise means the same as anticlockwise
